    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence presents a genuinely balanced risk-reward profile for AMZN. The bull case rests on solid structural technicals: an intact golden cross (50-day SMA at $183.01 above the 200-day SMA at $159.35), a fresh bullish MACD crossover, price holding above the 50-day SMA, and exceptional Q1 operating cash flow of $18.99B. However, the bear case is equally legitimate: flat 20-day price action (+0.02%), volume 25% below average, price below the 10-day EMA, capex consuming 94% of operating cash flow, two failed attempts at the $187-189 resistance zone, and critically, income statement data (revenue, margins, EPS) is unavailable from the supplied evidence, so profitability cannot be verified. With upside to $189 (~3%) roughly matching downside to $176 (~4%), the risk-reward is near 1:1, which does not justify a directional call. I maintain existing exposure at current levels (~$183.66) while awaiting a confirmed breakout above $189.50 on volume expansion (which would validate the bull) or a breakdown below $176-177 (which would validate the bear). Position sizing should remain at neutral/market-weight given the unverifiable fundamentals.\n\n**Entry Price**: 183.66\n\n**Stop Loss**: 176.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/market-weight exposure; do not add new capital at current levels\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
